SUMMARY:The Open Source Approach: Building Production-Ready AI Apps with P
 ostgres
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Postgres\n**WEBINAR:** It’s no secret that Postgres 
 is uniquely positioned as being an ideal foundation for agentic AI applica
 tions. However\, there are many different components you need to consider 
 to ensure your application runs as expected in an enterprise environment: 
 in a security hardened manner\, grounded in verifiable information\, with 
 efficient token usage.\n\nIn this talk\, we will show you how to leverage 
 the open source tools (licensed under the PostgreSQL license) within our p
 gEdge Agentic AI Toolkit to address these common concerns and ensure you
 ’re prepared for different architectural use cases.\nWe’ll cover at a 
 high level:\nThe pgEdge MCP Server for PostgreSQL\, a highly performant an
 d fully featured MCP server for access to any standard PostgreSQL database
 \, whether greenfield or pre-existing\nNatural Language Agents for queryin
 g data\, available via a command-line interface (CLI) or a web user interf
 ace (full-featured MCP clients written in Go\, with Anthropic prompt cachi
 ng for a 90% cost reduction)\npgEdge-vectorizer\, a Postgres extension tha
 t automatically chunks text content and generates vector embeddings using 
 background workers\npgEdge RAG Server\, a dedicated API Server for perform
 ing Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) of text based on content from a P
 ostgreSQL database using pgvector\npgEdge-docloader\, a utility that makes
  it easy to bring initial material online\nVectorChord-bm25\, a Postgres e
 xtension implementing BM25 ranked search for hybrid semantic and full-text
  searching\nBy the end of the session\, you will have insights on how to s
 afely deploy your AI applications to production while ensuring your data s
 overeignty\, privacy\, integrity\, security\, and performance is rock soli
 d.
